<title>USA: Magistrate recommends dropping potash suit - IMC.</title>
<headline>Magistrate recommends dropping potash suit - IMC.</headline>
<dateline>NORTHBROOK, Ill. 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The federal magistrate overseeing a civil antitrust suit alleging a price-fixing conspiracy in the potash industry has formally recommended the case be dismissed, IMC Global Inc said Monday.</p>
<p>Those named in the suit included IMC and Potash Corp of Saskatchewan, among others.</p>
<p>The U.S. Department of Justice had previously ended its grand jury investigation of the matter without action, IMC said.</p>
<p>The civil suit, pending in a Minnesota federal court, alleged a price-fixing conspiracy by U.S. and Canadian potash producers.</p>
<p>--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
